/-!
# The trianguline variety and its local model: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti. None of them is statable
there, so the file declares nothing; each headline is listed below with the carrier
it lacks.

* Framed almost de Rham and regular lattice completion equivalences (Layers 1–2):
  missing coefficient B_dR-representations of `G_K`, B_pdR, D_pdR, period lattices
  and their Artinian deformation groupoids. Mathlib's `BDeRhamPlus` and `BDeRham`
  are the bare period rings, with no Galois action, topology or generator `t`.
* Ordinary-flag dictionary and strictness and uniqueness of triangulations with
  an ordered-regular parameter (Layer 4): missing the coefficient Robba
  realization of continuous representations, saturated integral triangulations
  and their ordered parameters.
* Numerical Weil–Deligne criterion for noncritical triangulations (Layer 4):
  missing de Rham representations, Weil–Deligne flags and integral triangulations.
* The three rank-two de Rham triangulation cases (Layer 4): missing the de Rham
  and Weil–Deligne realization of a representation and its refinements.
* Formal smoothness of the filtered localized period comparison (Layer 5): missing
  localized Robba modules, period realization and the filtered deformation maps.
* Double-flag formal local model and normal component rings (Layer 6): missing the
  Robba deformation functors, the flag scheme of `Res_(K/ℚ_p) GL_n` and the
  Grothendieck incidence components.
* Galois component detection, indexing and tangent comparison (Layer 6): missing
  framed Galois deformation rings, the localized trianguline condition and its
  period and Cartan maps.
* Analytic completed local-model identification (Layer 7): missing the rigid
  trianguline variety, its completed local rings and the incidence local model.
* Local normality, Cohen–Macaulayness and character flatness (Layers 7–8): missing
  that variety, the rigid character spaces and its analytic character projections.
* Crystalline accumulation and the crystabelline companion criterion (Layer 8):
  missing crystabelline representations with their Weil–Deligne refinements,
  refined deformation spaces of fixed weight and abelian inertial type, their
  period-frame torsors and companion parameter points of the trianguline variety.
* Weight-fibre Kazhdan–Lusztig identity and full-character crystalline multiplicity
  formula (Layer 9): missing those analytic fibres, Kazhdan–Lusztig polynomials,
  Steinberg cycle transfer and locally analytic principal-series constituents.
* Injection-line recovery of crystabelline Hodge parameters (Layer 10): missing
  crystabelline Robba modules, their canonical endpoints and their period data.
* Surjectivity of single-embedding modification onto the crystabelline class
  with modified weights (Layer 10): missing crystabelline Robba modules and the
  embedding-selective period modification.
* Simultaneous-refinement derivative transport and paraboline product formulas
  (Layer 11): missing the Robba self-Ext spaces and refinement derivatives.
* Partial tangent modification and quotient comparison (Layer 12): missing
  embedding-selective Robba modification and partial de Rham extension spaces.
* Injection-image and matched-relation rigidity (Layer 13): missing those Robba
  Ext groups and their pullback and pushout maps.
* Higher intertwining and refinement tangent generation (Layer 13): missing the
  first/last filtration deformation spaces and rank-one infinitesimal twists.
* Original and single-embedding Hodge-recovery exact sequences (Layer 13): missing
  the higher-intertwining relations on the Robba tangent quotients.

The pinned matrix, module, scheme and algebraic-cycle carriers do not supply these
period or analytic moduli constructions. Linear-map identities about free vector
spaces and predicates on rational slopes would not state the listed headline
theorems, so none is written here in their place.
-/

